# Line endings for everything Terraform uploads to GCS, and for scripts.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default here) rewrites files as CRLF on
# checkout. Terraform compares file hashes, and GCS held a mix of LF and CRLF
# uploads — so a branch switch made unchanged objects show up as "changed"
# (2026-09-24: 8 of 30 planned changes were line endings only), which is
# exactly the noise a real, unwanted change hides in. Pinning LF makes every
# checkout byte-identical to what is committed, so a plan only lists real edits.
reports/**      text eol=lf
deploy/**       text eol=lf
terraform/*.tf  text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
.githooks/*     text eol=lf
